  "findings": [
    "EVERY subset job routed to full-tile by POLICY (fallback=None): merged terrain-aware influence bounds (elevation_offset_m = DEM relief; shadow length cap raised to the oracle march bound) enlarged dirty windows ~5x in area (S01 dirty fraction 0.0635 -> 0.3145 vs the 0.30 full_recompute_fraction threshold; S08 jobs likewise), so choose_recompute_mode selects FULL before any local solve. Under default InfluenceConfig the incremental local path is DEAD on this 500x500@2m site - no local job, hence the new 12 px margins were never exercised end-to-end. Direct consequence for P8/P5 tuning: the policy threshold vs terrain-aware influence bounds interaction needs review if local mode is meant to engage on real terrain.",
    "SCI-004 guard unobservable end-to-end (see gate finding): pre-merge the amaxvalue guard fired verbatim on S05; post-merge policy pre-empts it.",
    "Oracle path is code-invariant across the P5 remediation: all four recomputed merged-code oracles are bitwise identical to the pre-merge cached oracles for utci/tmrt/shadow (cross-check table in SANITY gate).",
    "The 12 px write margin (gvf_march_pixels(2.0)=11 +1) is confirmed in the merged worker, but no local write window was produced in this subset, so its end-to-end effect (window shrunk 23->12 px) could not be observed here; pre-merge T3 remains the evidence for local-mode correctness at 23 px, repo unit tests for the margin formula.",
    "Repo cache consumed directly (fixed solar_geometry.altitude_m=3.0); byte-identical (27/27 files) to the runner's cross-check cache /tmp/p5sci/cache_alt3."
  ],
